 "result_text": "I added a \"Delete All\" button to the contents view. It deletes every item in the folder, not just the 1000 shown on the current page. I only checked that the module imports. I didn't run the tests or try the button in a running Zope.\n\n- **Button:** `contents.dtml` now shows \"Delete All\" next to \"Delete\". It uses the same \"Delete objects\" permission check as the existing button, and it asks for confirmation in the browser before submitting.\n- **Method:** `BTreeFolder2.py` has a new `manage_delObjects_all`. It collects all the folder's ids and passes them to the existing `manage_delObjects`, so the normal removal events still fire. It then redisplays the contents view.\n- **Large folders:** all deletions happen in a single request and transaction, so a very large folder could be slow or hit memory limits.\n\nI didn't add any tests, as you asked.",
